== lit --help
Track projects, issues, comments and work claims. Commands never start the service.
Start with connect [--session NAME], then select a project with session set.
Session selection: --session > LIT_SESSION. Unnamed connect creates a random session.
Run a leaf command's --help
for required inputs, optional flags and valid combinations.

Usage:
  lit [flags]
  lit [command]

Available Commands:
  claims           Reserve issues with expiring work claims
  comments         Discuss issues with durable comments
  completion       Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  connect          Initialize or resume a client session
  disconnect       End a connected client session
  grep             Search current content using a literal substring
  help             Help about any command
  issues           Track work, state and relationships
  milestones       Group project issues into named worksets
  projects         Create and discover project containers
  search           Search current content ranked by relevance
  session          Inspect or change session preferences
  setup-skills     Install embedded skills for Codex or Claude
  transactions     Reconcile uncertain mutation outcomes
  tui              Open the terminal UI (lit-tui)
  version          Print the binary version
  workflow-session Bind explicit agent runtime sessions to lit clients

Flags:
      --endpoint URL       Optional. Service URL; flag > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411
      --format FORMAT      Optional. Output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json (otherwise session preference)
  -h, --help               help for lit
      --session NAME       Conditional. Logical session NAME; --session > LIT_SESSION; see requirements
      --timeout DURATION   Optional. Positive request DURATION, for example 30s (default 30s)

Use "lit [command] --help" for more information about a command.
== lit connect --help
Initialize or resume a client session.

Requirements:
  Required flags: none.
  Session: --session > LIT_SESSION; with neither, create a random throwaway session name.
  An explicitly supplied --session must not be empty; omit it to use the fallback.
  The result includes items[0].logical_session (Logical session in readable output). Reuse the returned name explicitly with --session NAME (or set LIT_SESSION).
  Throwaway describes the generated name; it does not imply automatic expiry or deletion.
  New sessions default to the system username (then USER, then human) and actor kind human.
  An existing local session resumes its saved client; --client-id adopts an existing client
  or must match that saved client. Optional actor/runtime/project flags update its properties.
  --format also saves the output preference here unless --output-format is explicit.
  Endpoint is optional: --endpoint > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411.
  --session-id-only prints only the logical session name plus a newline on success, not the client UUID.
  It overrides cli/markdown/json rendering for this call; --format and --output-format retain their normal preference effects.
  Errors and warnings go to stderr; failures return a nonzero status.

References:
  Project REF: exact title, UUID or unique UUID prefix.
  Use title:TITLE for literal title matching, or id:UUID_PREFIX for ID-only matching.

Valid forms:
  lit connect
  lit connect [--session NAME] [--actor-name NAME] [--actor-kind human|agent]
  lit connect [--session NAME] --client-id UUID [--project REF]
  lit connect [--session NAME] --format json --output-format cli
  lit connect [--session NAME] --session-id-only
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.

Usage:
  lit connect [flags]

Examples:
  lit connect --session my-session
  set -gx LIT_SESSION (lit connect --session-id-only)  # fish, current shell

Flags:
      --actor-kind KIND         Optional. Actor KIND: human or agent
      --actor-name NAME         Optional. Actor display NAME
      --client-id UUID          Optional. Existing client UUID to resume
  -h, --help                    help for connect
      --output-format FORMAT    Optional. Session output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json
      --project REF             Optional. Project REF: title or UUID; otherwise session selection
      --runtime-session-id ID   Optional. Vendor runtime session ID
      --runtime-vendor NAME     Optional. Runtime vendor NAME
      --session-id-only         Optional. Print only the logical session name and a newline on success; overrides output formatting, not saved preferences

Global Flags:
      --endpoint URL       Optional. Service URL; flag > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411
      --format FORMAT      Optional. Output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json (otherwise session preference)
      --session NAME       Conditional. Logical session NAME; --session > LIT_SESSION; see requirements
      --timeout DURATION   Optional. Positive request DURATION, for example 30s (default 30s)
== lit disconnect --help
End a connected client session.

Requirements:
  Required flag when LIT_SESSION is unset: --session NAME.
  Required session: --session NAME or LIT_SESSION; connect that session first.

Valid forms:
  lit disconnect [--session NAME]
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.

Usage:
  lit disconnect [flags]

Examples:
  lit disconnect --session my-session

Flags:
