Use "lit session [command] --help" for more information about a command.
== lit session get --help
Read session and current properties.

Requirements:
  No required property flags. Without property flags, show every session property, including the logical session name
  and its distinct client UUID. --session-id selects only the client UUID.
  Property selectors take no values.
  Required session: --session NAME or LIT_SESSION; connect that session first.

Valid forms:
  lit session get [--session NAME] [--project] [--actor-name] [--status]
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.

Usage:
  lit session get [flags]

Examples:
  lit session get --session my-session

Flags:
      --actor-kind           Optional. Show session property actor-kind
      --actor-name           Optional. Show session property actor-name
  -h, --help                 help for get
      --output-format        Optional. Show session property output-format
      --project              Optional. Show session property project
      --revision             Optional. Show session property revision
      --runtime-session-id   Optional. Show session property runtime-session-id
      --runtime-vendor       Optional. Show session property runtime-vendor
      --service-id           Optional. Show session property service-id
      --session-id           Optional. Show session property session-id
      --status               Optional. Show session property status

Global Flags:
      --endpoint URL       Optional. Service URL; flag > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411
      --format FORMAT      Optional. Output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json (otherwise session preference)
      --session NAME       Conditional. Logical session NAME; --session > LIT_SESSION; see requirements
      --timeout DURATION   Optional. Positive request DURATION, for example 30s (default 30s)
== lit session set --help
Set explicit session properties.

Requirements:
  Required: at least one property flag with a value.
  Properties: --project, --output-format, --actor-name, --actor-kind,
  --runtime-vendor, --runtime-session-id. Multiple properties may be set together.
  Required session: --session NAME or LIT_SESSION; connect that session first.

References:
  Project REF: exact title, UUID or unique UUID prefix.
  Use title:TITLE for literal title matching, or id:UUID_PREFIX for ID-only matching.

Valid forms:
  lit session set --project REF [--output-format cli|markdown|json]
  lit session set --actor-name NAME --actor-kind human|agent
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.

Usage:
  lit session set [flags]

Examples:
  lit session set --session my-session --project test/poc

Flags:
      --actor-kind KIND         Optional. Actor KIND: human or agent
      --actor-name NAME         Optional. Actor display NAME
  -h, --help                    help for set
      --output-format FORMAT    Optional individually; select at least one property. Session output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json
      --project REF             Optional individually; select at least one property. Project REF: title or UUID; otherwise session selection
      --runtime-session-id ID   Optional individually; select at least one property. Vendor runtime session ID
      --runtime-vendor NAME     Optional individually; select at least one property. Runtime vendor NAME

Global Flags:
      --endpoint URL       Optional. Service URL; flag > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411
      --format FORMAT      Optional. Output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json (otherwise session preference)
      --session NAME       Conditional. Logical session NAME; --session > LIT_SESSION; see requirements
      --timeout DURATION   Optional. Positive request DURATION, for example 30s (default 30s)
== lit session unset --help
Clear optional session properties.

Requirements:
  Required: at least one optional property selector (no value).
  Choose --project, --output-format, --runtime-vendor or --runtime-session-id.
  Actor name and kind cannot be unset.
  Required session: --session NAME or LIT_SESSION; connect that session first.

Valid forms:
  lit session unset --project [--output-format]
  lit session unset --runtime-vendor --runtime-session-id
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.

Usage:
  lit session unset [flags]

Examples:
  lit session unset --session my-session --project

Flags:
      --actor-kind           Optional. Clear session property actor-kind
      --actor-name           Optional. Clear session property actor-name
  -h, --help                 help for unset
      --output-format        Optional individually; select at least one property. Clear session property output-format
      --project              Optional individually; select at least one property. Clear session property project
      --runtime-session-id   Optional individually; select at least one property. Clear session property runtime-session-id
      --runtime-vendor       Optional individually; select at least one property. Clear session property runtime-vendor

Global Flags:
