== lit milestones --help
Group project issues into named worksets

Usage:
  lit milestones [flags]
  lit milestones [command]

Available Commands:
  create      Create milestones atomically
  get         Read milestones and current properties
  history     Read immutable mutation history
  list        List and filter milestones
  update      Update milestones atomically

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for milestones

Global Flags:
      --endpoint URL       Optional. Service URL; flag > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411
      --format FORMAT      Optional. Output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json (otherwise session preference)
      --session NAME       Conditional. Logical session NAME; --session > LIT_SESSION; see requirements
      --timeout DURATION   Optional. Positive request DURATION, for example 30s (default 30s)

Use "lit milestones [command] --help" for more information about a command.
== lit milestones create --help
Create milestones atomically.
Repeat the item boundary flag to submit an atomic batch, or use --file with a JSON array.
Scalar fields may occur once per item; repeated set fields preserve input order.

Requirements:
  Required: project selection via --project REF or the session, and --milestone TITLE per flag-defined item; or --file PATH (nonempty JSON array with project per item or selected project).
  Repeat --milestone to begin another atomic item; repeat --issue REF for members in that item. --issue references resolve within the milestone project.
  Content is optional. --content and --content-file are mutually exclusive per item; stdin (-) may be read only once.
  Required session: --session NAME or LIT_SESSION; connect that session first.

References:
  Milestone REF: exact title in the selected project, UUID, unique UUID prefix, title:TITLE, or id:UUID_PREFIX.
  Issue membership references resolve inside the selected milestone project.

Valid forms:
  lit milestones create [--project REF] --milestone TITLE [--content TEXT | --content-file PATH] [--issue REF...]
  lit milestones create [--project REF] --milestone TITLE [ITEM_FLAGS] --milestone TITLE [ITEM_FLAGS]
  lit milestones create --file PATH
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.
  FILTERS / ITEM_FLAGS / CHANGE_FLAGS refer to applicable flags below.

Usage:
  lit milestones create [flags]

Examples:
  lit milestones create --session my-session --project test/poc --milestone M1 --content 'Verify the PoC'

Flags:
      --content TEXT        Optional. UTF-8 content TEXT; conflicts with --content-file
      --content-file PATH   Optional. Read UTF-8 content from PATH; - reads stdin once
      --file PATH           Conditional (see valid forms). Input PATH: mutation JSON array or typed query object; - reads stdin once
  -h, --help                help for create
      --issue REF           Conditional (see valid forms). Existing issue REF to include in this milestone (repeatable within each item)
      --milestone TITLE     Conditional (see valid forms). Milestone TITLE (create: new title); repeat to begin another atomic item
      --project REF         Optional. Project REF: title or UUID; otherwise session selection

Global Flags:
      --endpoint URL       Optional. Service URL; flag > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411
      --format FORMAT      Optional. Output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json (otherwise session preference)
      --session NAME       Conditional. Logical session NAME; --session > LIT_SESSION; see requirements
      --timeout DURATION   Optional. Positive request DURATION, for example 30s (default 30s)
== lit milestones get --help
Read milestones and current properties.
With --format markdown, one complete returned record becomes YAML frontmatter
plus the exact original Markdown body. Duplicate selectors may return one record;
multiple returned records use a structured report. Export each separately for documents.
This is a read snapshot, not an import format: --content-file reads the entire file as body.

Requirements:
  Required: one or more milestone REF operands. Resolve the reference in the selected project.
  Milestone titles are resolved inside the selected project. A project-scoped UUID or ID prefix is valid; use the full UUID to avoid ambiguity.
  Required session: --session NAME or LIT_SESSION; connect that session first.

References:
  Milestone REF: exact title in the selected project, UUID, unique UUID prefix, title:TITLE, or id:UUID_PREFIX.
  Issue membership references resolve inside the selected milestone project.

Valid forms:
  lit milestones get REF...
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.

Usage:
  lit milestones get REF... [flags]

Examples:
  lit milestones get --session my-session --project test/poc M1

Flags:
  -h, --help          help for get
      --project REF   Optional. Project REF: title or UUID; otherwise session selection

Global Flags:
      --endpoint URL       Optional. Service URL; flag > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411
      --format FORMAT      Optional. Output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json (otherwise session preference)
      --session NAME       Conditional. Logical session NAME; --session > LIT_SESSION; see requirements
      --timeout DURATION   Optional. Positive request DURATION, for example 30s (default 30s)
== lit milestones list --help
List and filter milestones.
Filters combine with AND; set filters may repeat. --all conflicts with --limit/--cursor.
Reuse the same filters with a returned cursor. --all does not widen project scope.

Requirements:
  Required: project scope via --project REF, saved session selection, or project_id in the query file. Milestone queries cannot span projects.
  Choose flag filters or a typed JSON query object: cannot combine --file with query/filter flags.
  --all conflicts with --limit/--cursor; --all does not widen project scope.
  Reuse the same filters with --cursor. Filters combine with AND.
  Required session: --session NAME or LIT_SESSION; connect that session first.

References:
  Milestone REF: exact title in the selected project, UUID, unique UUID prefix, title:TITLE, or id:UUID_PREFIX.
  Issue membership references resolve inside the selected milestone project.

Valid forms:
  lit milestones list [--project REF] [FILTERS] [--limit N] [--cursor TOKEN]
  lit milestones list [--project REF] [FILTERS] --all
  lit milestones list --file PATH
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.
  FILTERS / ITEM_FLAGS / CHANGE_FLAGS refer to applicable flags below.

Usage:
  lit milestones list [flags]

Examples:
  lit milestones list --session my-session --project test/poc --limit 20

Flags:
      --all                      Optional. Return all results as one bounded snapshot; conflicts with --limit/--cursor
      --created-after RFC3339    Optional. Inclusive creation boundary RFC3339
      --created-before RFC3339   Optional. Exclusive creation boundary RFC3339
      --cursor TOKEN             Optional. Continue the same query with opaque TOKEN
      --direction DIRECTION      Optional. Sort DIRECTION: asc or desc
      --file PATH                Optional. Input PATH: mutation JSON array or typed query object; - reads stdin once
  -h, --help                     help for list
      --id UUID                  Optional. Match object UUID (repeatable)
      --limit N                  Optional. Page size N (default 100, maximum 1000 unless configured)
      --project REF              Optional. Project REF: title or UUID; otherwise session selection
  -q, --query TEXT               Optional. Case-insensitive content substring TEXT
      --sort FIELD               Optional. Sort FIELD: created-at, updated-at, title
      --title TITLE              Optional. Object TITLE (exact title filter on list)
      --updated-after RFC3339    Optional. Inclusive update boundary RFC3339
      --updated-before RFC3339   Optional. Exclusive update boundary RFC3339

Global Flags:
      --endpoint URL       Optional. Service URL; flag > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411
      --format FORMAT      Optional. Output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json (otherwise session preference)
      --session NAME       Conditional. Logical session NAME; --session > LIT_SESSION; see requirements
      --timeout DURATION   Optional. Positive request DURATION, for example 30s (default 30s)
== lit milestones update --help
Update milestones atomically.
Repeat the item boundary flag to submit an atomic batch, or use --file with a JSON array.
Scalar fields may occur once per item; repeated set fields preserve input order.

Requirements:
  Required: one or more milestone REF operands, or --file PATH (nonempty JSON array).
  Use --title, --content/--content-file, --add-issue, --remove-issue, --clear content|issues and --revision as needed. Member references resolve within each target milestone's project. --file cannot combine with flag or positional inputs. --content and --content-file are mutually exclusive per item; stdin (-) may be read only once.
  Milestone titles are resolved inside the selected project. A project-scoped UUID or ID prefix is valid; use the full UUID to avoid ambiguity.
  Required session: --session NAME or LIT_SESSION; connect that session first.

References:
  Milestone REF: exact title in the selected project, UUID, unique UUID prefix, title:TITLE, or id:UUID_PREFIX.
  Issue membership references resolve inside the selected milestone project.

Valid forms:
  lit milestones update REF... [CHANGE_FLAGS] [--revision N]
  lit milestones update --file PATH
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.
  FILTERS / ITEM_FLAGS / CHANGE_FLAGS refer to applicable flags below.

Usage:
  lit milestones update [REF...] [flags]

Examples:
  lit milestones update --session my-session --project test/poc M1 --content 'Updated details'

Flags:
      --add-issue REF       Optional. Add issue REF to milestone membership (repeatable)
      --clear FIELD         Optional. Clear FIELD (repeatable): content, issues
      --content TEXT        Optional. UTF-8 content TEXT; conflicts with --content-file
      --content-file PATH   Optional. Read UTF-8 content from PATH; - reads stdin once
      --file PATH           Conditional (see valid forms). Input PATH: mutation JSON array or typed query object; - reads stdin once
  -h, --help                help for update
      --project REF         Optional. Project REF: title or UUID; otherwise session selection
      --remove-issue REF    Optional. Remove issue REF from milestone membership (repeatable)
      --revision N          Optional. Expected object revision N; reject stale mutations
      --title TITLE         Optional. Object TITLE (exact title filter on list)

Global Flags:
      --endpoint URL       Optional. Service URL; flag > LIT_ENDPOINT > remembered session > http://127.0.0.1:7411
      --format FORMAT      Optional. Output FORMAT: cli, markdown or json (otherwise session preference)
      --session NAME       Conditional. Logical session NAME; --session > LIT_SESSION; see requirements
      --timeout DURATION   Optional. Positive request DURATION, for example 30s (default 30s)
