  The comment owner selector identifies the owning issue.
  Project REF: exact title, UUID or unique UUID prefix.
  Use title:TITLE for literal title matching, or id:UUID_PREFIX for ID-only matching.
  Issue REF: title in the selected project, UUID or unique UUID prefix.
  Use title:TITLE for a literal title, or id:UUID_PREFIX for ID-only matching.
  PROJECT_TITLE:ISSUE_REF selects an issue in another project, for example
  feat/api:title:Review API. A qualified prefix is scoped to that project;
  an unqualified UUID or ID prefix is global even when a project is selected.
  For titles containing slashes and colons, quote the argument and force title matching:
  --project test/poc 'title:Refactor a/b: cleanup'.

