== lit workflow-session run --help
Run a tracker command with the bound client.
Output is forwarded from the tracker command; the adapter supplies --format json.
Help and version retain their own text output.
Use the direct lit tracker command for CLI or Markdown output.

Requirements:
  Required flags: --host and --runtime-id.
  Required operand: a tracker COMMAND after --. connect is forbidden.
  The command cannot override --session, --endpoint, --client-id, --runtime-vendor,
  --runtime-session-id or --format; use the adapter lifecycle.
  Uses the saved runtime binding and endpoint; --endpoint and --project do not apply.

Valid forms:
  lit workflow-session --host codex|claude --runtime-id ID run -- COMMAND [ARGS...]
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.

Usage:
  lit workflow-session run -- COMMAND [ARGS...] [flags]

Examples:
  lit workflow-session --host codex --runtime-id SESSION run -- issues list

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for run

Global Flags:
      --cli EXECUTABLE   Optional. Path to lit EXECUTABLE (default: this binary)
      --host HOST        Required agent HOST: codex or claude
      --runtime-id ID    Required explicit vendor runtime session ID
== lit workflow-session checkout --help
Record a repository checkout path.
Output is a JSON association record; --format does not apply.

Requirements:
  Required flags: --host, --runtime-id, --repository and --path.
  Requires a saved session with a selected project.
  Uses the saved runtime binding and endpoint; --endpoint and --project do not apply.

Valid forms:
  lit workflow-session --host codex|claude --runtime-id ID checkout --repository REF --path DIRECTORY
  [] means optional; | separates alternatives; ... means repeatable.

Usage:
  lit workflow-session checkout [flags]

Examples:
  lit workflow-session --host codex --runtime-id SESSION checkout --repository github.com/example/repo --path /work/repo

Flags:
  -h, --help             help for checkout
      --path DIRECTORY   Required checkout DIRECTORY on this machine
      --repository REF   Required repository REF to associate with this checkout

Global Flags:
      --cli EXECUTABLE   Optional. Path to lit EXECUTABLE (default: this binary)
      --host HOST        Required agent HOST: codex or claude
      --runtime-id ID    Required explicit vendor runtime session ID
== lit completion --help
Generate the autocompletion script for lit for the specified shell: bash, fish or zsh.
See each sub-command's help for details on how to use the generated script.

Usage:
  lit completion [flags]
  lit completion [command]

Available Commands:
  bash        Generate the autocompletion script for bash
  fish        Generate the autocompletion script for fish
  zsh         Generate the autocompletion script for zsh

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for completion

Use "lit completion [command] --help" for more information about a command.
== lit completion bash --help
Generate the autocompletion script for bash (bash 4.4 or later).

To load completions in your current shell session:

	source <(lit completion bash)

To load completions for every new session, add that line to ~/.bashrc.

Usage:
  lit completion bash [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for bash
== lit completion fish --help
Generate the autocompletion script for fish (fish 3.4 or later).

To load completions in your current shell session:

	lit completion fish | source

To load completions for every new session, run once:

	lit completion fish > ~/.config/fish/completions/lit.fish

Usage:
  lit completion fish [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for fish
== lit completion zsh --help
Generate the autocompletion script for zsh (zsh 5.8 or later).

If shell completion is not already enabled in your environment, enable it once:

	autoload -U compinit; compinit

To load completions in your current shell session:

	source <(lit completion zsh)

To load completions for every new session, save the script as _lit in a directory on $fpath,
for example:

	lit completion zsh > "${fpath[1]}/_lit"

Start a new shell for this setup to take effect.

Usage:
  lit completion zsh [flags]

Flags:
  -h, --help   help for zsh
